g></svg></mjx-container>"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"When the gas is compressed suddenly, it undergoes an adiabatic process where no heat is exchanged with the surroundings.<br><br> Therefore, we can use the adiabatic equation of state to relate the initial and final pressure and volume of the gas: <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.063ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.838ex\" height=\"2.914ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -818.2 6116.5 1288\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(675,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\" transform=\"translate(1078.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(861.3,506.3) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D6FE\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FE\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(616,-297.3) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2651.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3707.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(675,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D453\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D453\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\" transform=\"translate(4821.3,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(8